cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
title: "Analysis code: Prognostic validity of disability and pain intensity by clinical examination at three-month follow-up in participants with acute neck pain"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Degenfellner
    given-names: "Jürgen"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6886-4583"
    affiliation: "Zurich University of Applied Sciences (ZHAW), School of Health Professions, Institute of Physiotherapy, Winterthur, Switzerland"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jdegenfellner/prognostic-validity-acute-neck-pain-code"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-09
keywords:
  - acute neck pain
  - prognostic model
  - best-subset regression
  - bootstrap validation
  - R
abstract: >-
  R code for all analyses reported in the manuscript "Prognostic validity of
  Disability and Pain Intensity by clinical examination at Three-Month
  Follow-Up in Participants with Acute Neck Pain: A Prospective Cohort Study"
  (Ernst, Degenfellner, Gmünder, Morf, Reicherzer, Hotz Boendermaker; ZHAW).
  Includes variable derivation, missingness handling, kNN imputation,
  best-subset regression with BIC selection, and bootstrap internal
  validation. Individual participant data are not included.
